.TH PAPERWEIGHT\-VOLUME 1 "2026-11-08" "paperweight-skel 0.2.87" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
paperweight\-volume \- raise or lower the output volume
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B paperweight\-volume
.BR up | down
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B paperweight\-volume
changes the volume of the default PipeWire output by 5% using
.BR wpctl (1).
It unmutes the output first, so pressing a volume key always gives sound.
.PP
The laptop volume keys run it, including while the screen is locked.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.B up
Raise the volume by 5%, up to a limit of 200%.
.TP
.B down
Lower the volume by 5%.
.PP
With any other argument, or none, it only unmutes the output.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wpctl (1),
.BR pavucontrol (1)
